 "prompt": "The repository at /testbed has a bug, described below. Fix it by changing the source code; do not modify or\nadd tests. When you are done, the project's existing test suite should pass.\n\n<issue>\nAccessTokenEndpoint missing BaseEndpoint inheritance breaks validation methods\n\n#### Description\n\nThe AccessTokenEndpoint class is missing inheritance from BaseEndpoint, causing validation methods to fail when creating access token responses.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nfrom oauthlib.oauth1 import RequestValidator\nfrom oauthlib.oauth1.rfc5849.endpoints import AccessTokenEndpoint\n\nclass MockValidator(RequestValidator):\n    def validate_timestamp_and_nonce(self, client_key, timestamp, nonce, request, request_token=None):\n        return True\n    \n    def validate_client_key(self, client_key, request):\n        return True\n        \n    def validate_request_token(self, client_key, token, request):\n        return True\n        \n    def validate_verifier(self, client_key, token, verifier, request):\n        return True\n        \n    def validate_signature(self, client_key, client_secret, resource_owner_key, resource_owner_secret, request):\n        return True\n        \n    def get_access_token(self, client_key, token, request):\n        return 'access_token', 'access_secret'\n\nvalidator = MockValidator()\nendpoint = AccessTokenEndpoint(validator)\n\n# This should work but fails\nuri = 'https://example.com/access_token'\nheaders = {'Authorization': 'OAuth oauth_consumer_key=\"foo\", oauth_token=\"token\", oauth_verifier=\"verifier\", oauth_signature_method=\"HMAC-SHA1\", oauth_timestamp=\"1234567890\", oauth_nonce=\"abc123\", oauth_signature=\"signature\"'}\n\nh, b, s = endpoint.create_access_token_response(uri, headers=headers)\n```\n\nThe endpoint fails to properly validate requests because it's missing essential methods from BaseEndpoint.\n</issue>\n",
